.TH SYS_VM_INFO 2 "2026-05-09" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_vm_info \- query VM zone-level memory breakdown
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_vm_info(sys_vminfo_t *" info ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_vm_info ()
fills
.I *info
with per-zone physical memory totals and free counts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
typedef struct sys_vminfo {
    uint64_t dma_total;     uint64_t dma_free;
    uint64_t normal_total;  uint64_t normal_free;
    uint64_t highmem_total; uint64_t highmem_free;
} sys_vminfo_t;
.fi
.RE
.PP
Substrate today maintains a single physical zone — the buddy
allocator covers all memory below
.BR PMM_DIRECTMAP_PHYS_LIMIT .
The whole pool is therefore reported under
.B normal_total
/
.BR normal_free ,
with
.B dma_*
and
.B highmem_*
zeroed.  When zone splitting lands the same syscall begins
populating the other zones; the layout is forward-compatible.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success; on failure -1 and
.I errno
is set per the error contract
.RB ( docs/syscalls/error-contract.md ).
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I info
is NULL.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I info
points outside the caller's address space.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_vm_stats (2),
.BR sys_vm_swap (2),
.BR sys_vm_buffers (2),
.BR sys_vm_slabs (2),
.BR sysinfo (2)
